# N3 example: stratified-negation.
# Companion to stratified-negation.eye/.srl: the producer of :blocked
# appears after its consumer deliberately. N3 has no stratification
# concept of its own; its negation-as-failure feature (log:notIncludes)
# is instead handled by deferring the negated rule until the ordinary
# closure saturates.

@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#>.
@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyepl/examples/stratified-negation#>.

:alice a :Person.
:bob a :Person.
:carol a :Person.
:alice a :DirectlyBlocked.
:carol a :Flagged.

{?x a :DirectlyBlocked} => {?x a :Blocked}.
{?x a :Flagged} => {?x a :Blocked}.

{?x a :Person. ?SCOPE log:notIncludes {?x a :Blocked}.} => {?x a :Eligible}.
